          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In the language of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theory
            the ordinary definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            has the following simple re-formulation:
          %p
            In a given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            is an object which is
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-connective"}> 1-connective
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-truncated"}> 1-truncated
                \.
          %p There are various evident generalizations of this, where one allows the degree in either of the two clauses to vary. In the literature one finds higher gerbes defined in either way, and so there are more general and more specific definitions.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#general General
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mover
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \overline{\mathbb{N}}
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+natural+number"} extended natural number
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                    \-gerbe
                  is an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mo ∈
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} \in \mathbf{G}
                  that is
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-connective"}> 1-connective
                      ;
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated"}> n-truncated
                      \.
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %strong
                    EM
                    = succeed "-gerbe" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  is an an
                  = succeed "-gerbe" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connective"} n-connective
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated"}> n-truncated
                      \.
          %p
            The definition of “EM
            = succeed "-gerbes\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, def. 7.2.2.20
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            the definition of “general
            = succeed "-gerbe\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em nonabelian 2-gerbe
            at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-gerbe"} 2-gerbe
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Breen"} Breen
          %p In particular we have then the following.
          #InfinityGerbe.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-gerbe
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-connective"} connected
              object.
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Gerbe
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\infty Gerbe \subset \mathcal{X}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
              of the full-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              on the
              = succeed "-gerbes." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .num_remark
            %h6#warning Warning
            %p
              The notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              between EM
              = succeed "-gerbes" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, pages 576, 577
              is more restrictive than this. This is the reason why the classification found there is a restriction of the general classification. This is discussed
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Properties"} below
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If one adds to the definition of “EM
              = succeed "-gerbe\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              has a “global section”, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒢
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to \mathcal{G}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+object"} Eilenberg-MacLane object
              in degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-gerbes" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p
              By the main theorem at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
              the connected
              %em and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
              objects in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              are equivalently (the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
              objects: we have an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒳
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Ω
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒳
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Omega \dashv \mathbf{B})
                    \:
                    \\infty Grp(\mathcal{X})
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\Omega}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\mathbf{B}}{\to}}
                    \\mathcal{X}_{*, \geq 1}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore an
              = succeed "-gerbe" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of an
              = succeed "-group," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %p But notice that a section always exists locally: for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mo *
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (x^* \dashv x_*) : \infty Grpd
                    \\stackrel{\overset{x^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{x_*}{\to}}
                    \\mathcal{X}
            %p
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} topos point
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \in \mathcal{X}
              an
              = succeed "-gerbe," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^* P \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^*
              preserves the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} categorical homotopy groups in an (∞,1)-topos
              and preserves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                    %mi P
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x^* P \simeq B G_x
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore it is natural to consider the notion of an
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                \-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-gerbe
              for a fixed
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ∈
